1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,540
Imagine waking up tomorrow and discovering
that India can no longer trade with China.

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:08,130
China is one of India's biggest
sources of imported goods.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,737
In financial year 2024–25,

4
00:00:09,970 --> 00:00:15,290
India imported around $113 billion
worth of merchandise from China.

5
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,320
Think about electronics,

6
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:20,460
machinery, chemicals and components
used in industries across India.

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,910
Many businesses depend
on these supply chains.

8
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,490
If trade suddenly stopped, companies
would need alternative suppliers.

9
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:28,760
Some products could become more expensive,

10
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:32,400
factories could face shortages,
and supply chains would need to adjust.

11
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,130
But there's another problem
India faces every November,

12
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:37,030
and you can literally see it from space.

